Subject: [PATCH 5/5] SHMQ 3-level {FP16, INT8, INT4} quantization for T4 (sm_75)

This patch adds a new vLLM quantization method `shmq_3level` that supports
3-level mixed-precision weights {FP16, INT8, INT4} in a single Linear layer.

Key features:
  - Works on T4 (sm_75, Turing) — relaxes MixLLM's min_capability from 80 to 75
  - Uses cupy.RawKernel + NVRTC for the 3-level fused GEMM (compiled at runtime)
  - SINGLE kernel launch for all 3 precision levels (no cuBLAS split for FP16)
  - PTX MMA wrappers defined for all 3 Turing tensor core types:
      * mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k16.row.col.f32.f16.f16.f32  (FP16)
      * mma.sync.aligned.m8n8k16.row.col.s32.s8.s8.s32      (INT8)
      * mma.sync.aligned.m8n8k4.row.col.s32.s4.s4.s32       (INT4)  <-- Turing-specific
  - CUDA cores path as default (guaranteed correctness); tensor-core path
    available via -DSHMQ_USE_TENSOR_CORES=1 compile flag
  - Falls back to PyTorch dequant + matmul when cupy is unavailable
  - Compatible with Qwen2 / Qwen2.5 / Llama architectures
  - Reads quantization config from `shmq_config.json` saved by SHMQ-Ultimate pipeline

Usage:
  vllm serve Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct-SHMQ \\
      --quantization shmq_3level \\
      --dtype float16 \\
      --gpu-memory-utilization 0.9

Or programmatically:
  from vllm import LLM
  llm = LLM(model="Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct-SHMQ",
            quantization="shmq_3level",
            dtype="float16",
            enforce_eager=True)  # T4 may need eager mode

The SHMQ-Ultimate quantization artifact is created by:
  python -m shmq.pipeline --config configs/qwen7b_3level.json

The artifact contains:
  - model.safetensors (weights in FP16/INT8/INT4 packed format)
  - shmq_config.json (per-layer bit-width, permutation, cluster sizes)
  - the standard Qwen2 config.json + tokenizer

This patch is applied ON TOP of MixLLM's vLLM patches 0001-0004 (which add
the W4.4A8 2-level MixLLM method). Our `shmq_3level` method is independent
and does not interfere with MixLLM's `mixllm` method.
